Sign in and store your snouty configuration

Sign in to your tenant, then save the tenant and its container registry in the
global snouty settings file and store your credential. Login checks the
credential with the tenant, and saves nothing when the tenant rejects it.
Information not provided via args is asked for at the terminal. Without a
terminal, login checks the credential that other commands use, such as
ANTITHESIS_API_KEY, and stores no credential.

Usually login saves the registry that your tenant reports,
`registry.<tenant>.antithesis.com`, and you do not need --registry. When another
registry is saved for the tenant, login asks whether to replace it, and the
default keeps it. Without a terminal, login keeps it. When the tenant reports
none, login asks for the registry at the terminal, or keeps the one saved for
that tenant. Use --registry to push your images to a different registry, such as
`registry.example.com/team`: a host, optionally with a port and a path. That
registry must be registered with your Antithesis tenant or provided by
Antithesis. If you are not sure, contact Antithesis support. Then sign in to
that registry with `docker login` or `podman login`.

NOTE: `snouty login` will offer to reuse your existing configuration values,
including any sourced from the file specified by --settings or via the
SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH environment variable. However, snouty login will save the
specified configuration and credentials to the "global" files in your home
directory.

Examples:
  snouty login
  snouty login --tenant "mytenant" --registry "registry.example.com/team"

Usage: snouty login [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --tenant <TENANT>
          Your Antithesis tenant, such as acme

      --registry <REGISTRY>
          The container registry to push your images to, in place of the
          tenant's registry

      --base-url <BASE_URL>
          The URL to sign in at, in place of https://<tenant>.antithesis.com.
          Login saves it as the base_url setting

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to a settings file that overrides the global settings file
          (overrides SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)
